---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SkinMap from '../components/SkinMap.astro';
import ShelfAudit from '../components/ShelfAudit.astro';
import { href } from '../data/site';
import { topics } from '../data/topics';
import { sources } from '../data/sources';
import { fieldNotes } from '../data/field-guide';
---
<Layout title="Skin is weird. Care can be simple.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow hero-kicker"><span aria-hidden="true">✳</span> A field guide for the skin you’re in</span>
        <h1>Skin is weird.<br />Care can be<br /><em>simple.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">Tiny pores. Busy microbes. A bathroom shelf with main-character energy. Let’s get curious about what your skin actually needs—and make a little room for less.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-dark" href="#shelf">Give my routine a rethink <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link fine" href="#skin-basics">First, meet your skin <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
        <p class="hero-small">Useful care. No purity contest. Absolutely no checkout cart.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero-art">
        <span class="art-label">Fig. 00 / At home in your own skin</span>
        <div class="hero-sticker" aria-hidden="true">Pores included.<strong>Obviously.</strong></div>
        <img src={href('images/bath.webp')} width="1100" height="825" alt="A contented peach-colored character with dotted skin relaxes in a lilac bathtub and gives a peace sign." fetchpriority="high" />
        <figcaption class="hero-caption">No serum was harmed in the making of this good mood.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="ticker"><div class="wrap ticker-inner"><span>Comfort over perfection</span><span class="ticker-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span>Curiosity with receipts</span><span class="ticker-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span>Keep the sunscreen</span></div></div>
  <section class="section intro-section"><div class="wrap intro-grid">
    <div><span class="eyebrow mb-5">A smaller routine. A bigger question.</span><h2>What if we don’t<br />need all <em>this stuff?</em></h2></div>
    <div class="intro-copy"><p>Wash. Scrub. Tone. Layer. Repeat. It’s easy for care to turn into a part-time job. Which steps help, which do we enjoy, and which just came with persuasive packaging?</p><p>Free the Pores explores simpler skin care with a soft spot for human weirdness and a healthy appetite for footnotes. Keep useful hygiene, sun protection, and treatment. Question the automatic extras.</p><a class="text-link fine inline-block mt-5" href={href('why/')}>The idea behind the name <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section skin-section" id="skin-basics"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Your skin, in three little pieces</span><h2>A whole neighborhood.<br /><em>Already at work.</em></h2></div><p class="section-aside">The picture is playful.<br />The biology is worth understanding.</p></div>
    <SkinMap />
  </div></section>
  <section class="section" id="shelf"><div class="wrap"><ShelfAudit /></div></section>
  <section class="section questions" id="questions"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Seven ways to get curious</span><h2>Let’s get under<br /><em>the surface.</em></h2></div><a class="text-link fine shrink-0" href={href('research/#library')}>{sources.length} sources. No secret sauce. ↗</a></div>
    <div class="question-list">{topics.map((topic, i) => <a class="question-row" href={href(`research/${topic.slug}/`)}><span class="question-number">0{i + 1}</span><span class="question-glyph" aria-hidden="true">{fieldNotes[topic.slug].icon}</span><div><span class="eyebrow">{topic.label}</span><h3>{topic.title}</h3></div><p>{topic.description}</p><span class="row-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}</div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section reality-section"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">A small reality check</span><h2>Sounds good.<br /><em>Does it hold water?</em></h2></div><p class="section-aside">Open a claim. Peek at the catch.</p></div>
    <div class="reality-grid">
      <details><summary><span class="eyebrow">The label says</span>“Natural means gentle.”<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>A plant can smell lovely and still trigger contact allergy. The ingredient, formula, dose, and person matter more than the leaf on the label.</p><a class="text-link" href={href('research/natural/')}>Read past the leaf ↗</a></details>
      <details><summary><span class="eyebrow">The internet says</span>“More microbes = better skin.”<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>A changed microbial sample is not automatically a health benefit. Look for outcomes like symptoms and barrier function, not just a bigger bacterial guest list.</p><a class="text-link" href={href('research/microbiome/')}>Meet the evidence ↗</a></details>
      <details><summary><span class="eyebrow">The plot twist</span>“Minimalists can use products.”<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Yes. Useful care gets to stay. Moisturizer, sunscreen, conditioner, and a prescribed treatment can all belong in a simple routine.</p><a class="text-link" href={href('research/useful-products/')}>Meet the keepers ↗</a></details>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section bottom-cta"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">No starter kit required</span><h2>Less shelf.<br /><em>More self.</em></h2><p>Choose one optional step. Notice what helps. Leave room to change your mind—and ask for help when your skin needs it.</p><a class="button button-dark" href={href('less/')}>Try a little less <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="fine cta-footnote">An independent exploration by Christopher Smothers.<br /><a href={href('about/')}>Our research standards are here, in normal-sized type.</a></p></div></section>
</Layout>
